      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "1. Meaning of Economic Planning"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Economic planning in India was aimed at achieving growth, modernization, self-reliance, and social justice.",
        "The Planning Commission was established in 1950 to formulate India's Five-Year Plans.",
        "A total of 12 Five-Year Plans were implemented before the system was restructured.",
        "In 2015, NITI Aayog replaced the Planning Commission to serve as a policy think tank promoting cooperative federalism."
      ],
      "id": "tq1ajxn"
    },
